OrionLayer open fix 107 — the evolutionary mutation on the wire
===============================================================

Work order 318 ("the evolutionary mutation"). orion2re on the fork's
branch `orionlayer` (v2.0.0), on top of open fix 106; commit ec66171a. Not
on `orionlayer-local`. In src/game/raceopt.cpp and src/ext/ext_api.cpp
under ORION2RE_EXT.

raceopt::Evolutionary_Mutation_Screen (raceopt.cpp:213; the lines are
v2.0.0's, before this fix moved them), the human
player's branch of Setup_Evolutionary_Upgrade (:188-211, from
report.cpp:537 when Evolutionary Mutation is researched), is the Custom
Race screen in mutation mode and ran under the galaxy map's id 0 with
nothing on the wire but its fields and its message boxes. From the first
Add_Race_Options_Fields_EM (:253) to the end of its loop a TurnPopupGuard
reports id 83 and TPOP kind 23: args [0] orig_picks (Calculate_EM_Picks:
starting + mutation_bonus less the race's costs), [1]..[10] the baseline
flags 0-9 (:223-232): flag 0 (args[1]) is the government's trait value,
traits[0] & 0x0E (:200), not a pick index; group g's flag is
baseline[g + 1], i.e. args[g + 2] — its level 1-3 where the race's trait
matches one, else the raw trait byte (:226-232). The tail, written on every snapshot from raceopt's
globals because each input changes them and Add_Race_Options_Fields_EM
adds the fields again (:402): int16 picks, int16 negative_picks, 10 x
int16 button_variable, 22 x int16 option_toggle, 36 x int16 group_button
(group g's level l at [g * 4 + l], [g * 4] -1000), 22 x int16
option_button, int16 accept; -1000 a field not added (not offered). The
opening box (KEN 77 + 78, :269-273) and the refusals (KEN 73-75) stand
over it as MSGB (kind 1, the refusals kind 4). Ended right after the loop, before the fields are
released. Read only.

Live: UNVERIFIED — no live run (Data's decision of 20 October 2026); built
and compiled (`linux-debug`, ORION2RE_EXT on; raceopt.cpp also without
it; a misspelt member refused by the compiler on the scratch clone).

